# Storybook — storefront only

Storybook lives in **`apps/storefront`**. It documents **storefront UI components** (Next.js), not Medusa Admin (`apps/backend/src/admin`).

Run:
```bash
npm run storefront:storybook   # from monorepo root
cd apps/storefront && npm run storybook
```

Build static docs: `cd apps/storefront && npm run build-storybook`

Official references:
- https://storybook.js.org/docs
- CSF3: https://storybook.js.org/docs/api/csf
- Args: https://storybook.js.org/docs/writing-stories/args
- Next.js + Vite: `@storybook/nextjs-vite` (configured in `.storybook/main.ts`)

---

# Component design for Storybook

## Presentational first

Components shown in Storybook must be **presentational**:
- All visible copy, images, and links come from **props / args**
- No `fetch`, no Medusa SDK, no React context that requires the real app
- Data fetching and country-code routing stay in **page wrappers** or small utils (see `buildLandingHeroProps`)

```tsx
// ✅ Page (server) — connected
<LandingHero {...buildLandingHeroProps(countryCode, DEFAULT_LANDING_HERO_CONTENT)} />

// ✅ Story — presentational, args only
export const Default: Story = {}
```

## File layout (co-location)

Place stories next to the component:

```
src/modules/landing/components/hero/
  index.tsx              # component (default export)
  hero.types.ts          # exported prop types
  hero-content.ts        # default copy / fixture data for prod + stories
  hero-utils.ts          # optional: page-only helpers (country code, etc.)
  hero.stories.tsx       # Storybook CSF file
```

Naming: **`{component-name}.stories.tsx`** beside `index.tsx`.

Title hierarchy mirrors product structure: `Landing/Hero`, `Products/Thumbnail`, `Skeletons/SkeletonButton`.

