# Story format — CSF3

Use **Component Story Format 3** with TypeScript `satisfies`:

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from "@storybook/nextjs-vite"
import LandingHero from "./index"
import { DEFAULT_LANDING_HERO_CONTENT } from "./hero-content"

const meta = {
  title: "Landing/Hero",
  component: LandingHero,
  tags: ["autodocs"],
  parameters: { layout: "fullscreen" },
  args: DEFAULT_LANDING_HERO_CONTENT,
} satisfies Meta<typeof LandingHero>

export default meta
type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>

export const Default: Story = {}
```

Rules:
- **Prefer `args`** over hard-coded props or custom `render` functions
- Omit `render` when the story only spreads args into the component
- Put **shared default args** on `meta.args` (component level), not duplicated per story
- Name stories by **state or use case**: `Default`, `WithoutBackgroundImage`, `Mobile` — not `RedVariant`
- Use **`...story.args` spread** to extend a sibling story when needed (CSF3 reuse)

Do **not** use CSF2 `Template.bind({})` for new stories.

