# Args, controls, and fixtures

| Pattern | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `hero.types.ts` | Exported TypeScript props — drives autodocs prop table |
| `hero-content.ts` | `DEFAULT_*` constants + **presets** (copy, images) |
| `hero.story-args.ts` | **Flat args** for Controls + `storyArgsToHeroProps()` mapper |
| `hero.mdx` | User-facing customization guide (optional) |
| `meta.argTypes` | Grouped controls (`table.category`), `if` for conditional fields |
| `meta.render` | Map flat story args → component props when Controls UX needs flattening |

## Flat args pattern (complex components)

When props are nested (`primaryCta: { label, href }`), object controls are hard for non-devs. Use flat story args:

```tsx
// hero.story-args.ts
export function storyArgsToHeroProps(args: LandingHeroStoryArgs): LandingHeroProps { ... }

// hero.stories.tsx
render: (args) => <LandingHero {...storyArgsToHeroProps(args)} />,
argTypes: {
  primaryCtaLabel: { name: "Nhãn nút chính", table: { category: "🔘 Nút bấm" } },
  showSecondaryCta: { control: "boolean" },
}
```

Add **presets** in `*-content.ts` and a `contentPreset` select control for one-click switching.

- Keep fixtures **deterministic** — no real network calls in stories
- For images in stories, use stable URLs (e.g. Unsplash with fixed params, picsum seed)
- Export default content from `*-content.ts` so production and Storybook stay in sync

