# Layout, viewports, and responsive

Global preview: `apps/storefront/.storybook/preview.tsx` imports `src/styles/globals.css` (Tailwind + Medusa tokens).

Per-story `parameters.layout`:
| Layout | When |
|--------|------|
| `fullscreen` | Hero, page sections, nav |
| `padded` | Cards, buttons, small widgets |
| `centered` | Icons, isolated atoms (use sparingly) |

**Mobile-first:** add viewport stories for key landing components:

```tsx
export const Mobile: Story = {
  parameters: { viewport: { defaultViewport: "mobile1" } },
}
```

Test at 375px, 768px, 1280px for new landing/marketing components.

When adding stories, update `tailwind.config.js` `content` if new paths are outside existing globs (already includes `./src/**/*.stories.*`).

---

# Decorators and app context

Use **decorators** for context (theme, router, padding wrapper) — **not** extra props on the component API.

```tsx
// Story-level wrapper
export const Narrow: Story = {
  decorators: [(Story) => <div className="max-w-sm"><Story /></div>],
}
```

- **Next.js routing / `next/link`:** handled by `@storybook/nextjs-vite` (`parameters.nextjs.appDirectory: true` in preview)
- **Do not** pass router mocks as component props
- For components that need `useParams()` (e.g. `LocalizedClientLink`), prefer a **presentational variant** with plain `<a href>` in the landing module, or wrap with a story decorator — avoid coupling Storybook to country-code context unless necessary

Global decorators belong in `.storybook/preview.tsx` only when every story needs them.

---

# Args composition (pages / composites)

For screens built from sub-components, reuse **fixture objects**, not imported stories:

```tsx
// ✅ Share content constants
args: {
  ...DEFAULT_LANDING_HERO_CONTENT,
  title: "Custom title",
}

// ❌ Avoid importing another story file (decorators/context won't apply)
// import { Default as HeroDefault } from "./hero.stories"
```

Reference: https://storybook.js.org/docs/writing-stories/build-pages-with-storybook

